074},1785612822.482632,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1073},{\"_345\":346,\"_333\":26,\"_347\":14,\"_296\":866,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":867,\"_302\":867,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1067,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},[335],{},{\"_255\":1067,\"_262\":1078,\"_35\":1079,\"_266\":1080,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1081,\"_275\":276},\"7b878541-3f32-43f4-9cb3-b79cb96c6bca\",[1057],{\"_322\":336,\"_273\":1083},1785612821.617171,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1082},{\"_333\":26,\"_296\":866,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":867,\"_302\":867,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1076,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},[335],{},{\"_255\":1076,\"_262\":1087,\"_35\":1088,\"_266\":1089,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":331,\"_273\":1090,\"_275\":276},\"c62f3fa5-1645-427b-87ba-4f92cd49de2c\",[1067],{\"_322\":336,\"_273\":1093},1785612822.466888,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1092},{\"_345\":1091,\"_333\":26,\"_296\":866,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":867,\"_302\":867,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1085,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},\"attachment_caas_paths_v1\",[335],{},{\"_255\":1085,\"_262\":1097,\"_35\":1098,\"_37\":1099,\"_266\":1100,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1101,\"_275\":276},\"b1161fe6-a6bc-4c2a-99ac-20a5739388ca\",[1076],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1115},1785612819.079,1785612834.445419,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1113},{\"_1102\":1103,\"_632\":1104,\"_296\":866,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":867,\"_302\":867,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},\"attachments\",[1106],{\"_634\":1105},[],{\"_255\":716,\"_1107\":1108,\"_440\":715,\"_1109\":1110,\"_717\":1111,\"_721\":722,\"_1112\":14},\"size\",815250,\"mime_type\",\"application/pdf\",\"local\",\"is_big_paste\",[1114],\"this is synopsis of previous idea i want the synopsis of this project\",{},{\"_255\":1095,\"_262\":1119,\"_35\":1120,\"_37\":1121,\"_266\":1122,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1123,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"283e56ba-5a73-4a73-8f91-cad968fa49cd\",[1085],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1143},1785528136.174995,1785528147.824508,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1141},{\"_279\":1124,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1125,\"_284\":1126,\"_286\":1127,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1128,\"_294\":1129,\"_296\":1130,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1131,\"_302\":1131,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1117,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1140},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1132,\"_581\":1133,\"_583\":1134,\"_585\":1135},[],\"a904096f-26d3-4700-971c-9880bea30ca6\",\"7328a26f-4665-4d13-9819-5a36acac63aa\",{\"_255\":1139,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1138,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1137,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1136,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"8704cy\",\"swl7t3\",\"0rn4p0\",\"h85il1\",[316],[1142],\"Absolutely. This is where we'll start writing the **actual project**, but I want to set one rule that will save us from a lot of problems later.\\n\\n## We are not going to \\\"code and hope.\\\"\\n\\nWe'll follow a professional sprint workflow.\\n\\n```\\nDesign\\n   ↓\\nImplementation\\n   ↓\\nTesting\\n   ↓\\nDocumentation\\n   ↓\\nZIP Update\\n```\\n\\nEvery sprint ends with:\\n- ✅ Working code\\n- ✅ Updated documentation\\n- ✅ Updated diagrams (if needed)\\n- ✅ Updated ZIP package\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🚀 Sprint 1.1 – Project Initialization\\n\\nThis sprint's goal is **not** to build features.\\n\\nIts goal is to create the foundation that every future feature depends on.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n```\\nSprint 1.1\\n\\n✅ Project Folder Structure\\n✅ Python Virtual Environment\\n✅ Git Repository\\n✅ requirements.txt\\n✅ Flask App Factory\\n✅ Configuration\\n✅ Environment Variables\\n✅ Logging\\n✅ Database Connection\\n✅ SQLAlchemy\\n✅ Flask-Migrate\\n✅ Base Template\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 📁 Final Folder Structure\\n\\nThis is the structure we'll actually implement.\\n\\n```text\\nFinPilotAI/\\n│\\n├── app/\\n│   ├── __init__.py\\n│   ├── config.py\\n│   │\\n│   ├── auth/\\n│   │   ├── __init__.py\\n│   │   ├── routes.py\\n│   │   ├── forms.py\\n│   │   ├── services.py\\n│   │   └── templates/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── dashboard/\\n│   ├── documents/\\n│   ├── ai/\\n│   ├── reports/\\n│   ├── chat/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── models/\\n│   │   ├── user.py\\n│   │   ├── document.py\\n│   │   ├── document_analysis.py\\n│   │   ├── report.py\\n│   │   └── chat_history.py\\n│   │\\n│   ├── services/\\n│   │   ├── ai_service.py\\n│   │   ├── ocr_service.py\\n│   │   ├── report_service.py\\n│   │   └── upload_service.py\\n│   │\\n│   ├── templates/\\n│   │   ├── base.html\\n│   │   ├── includes/\\n│   │   ├── layouts/\\n│   │   └── components/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── static/\\n│   │   ├── css/\\n│   │   ├── js/\\n│   │   ├── images/\\n│   │   ├── icons/\\n│   │   └── fonts/\\n│   │\\n│   └── utils/\\n│\\n├── migrations/\\n├── uploads/\\n├── logs/\\n├── tests/\\n├── docs/\\n├── instance/\\n│\\n├── run.py\\n├── requirements.txt\\n├── .env\\n├── .gitignore\\n├── README.md\\n└── LICENSE\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🛠️ Technology Stack (Locked)\\n\\n## Backend\\n\\n- Python 3.13+\\n- Flask\\n- SQLAlchemy\\n- Flask-Migrate\\n- Flask-Login\\n- Flask-WTF\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Database\\n\\n- MySQL 8\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Frontend\\n\\n- HTML5\\n- CSS3\\n- Bootstrap 5\\n- JavaScript (ES6)\\n- Jinja2\\n\\n---\\n\\n## AI\\n\\n- Tesseract OCR\\n- OpenAI-compatible API\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Charts\\n\\n- Chart.js\\n\\n---\\n\\n## File Storage\\n\\n- Local Uploads (Version 1)\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🧩 Architecture (Locked)\\n\\nWe are using a layered architecture.\\n\\n```\\nBrowser\\n      │\\n      ▼\\nRoutes (Blueprints)\\n      │\\n      ▼\\nServices\\n      │\\n      ▼\\nModels\\n      │\\n      ▼\\nMySQL\\n```\\n\\nEvery request will follow this flow.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 📋 Coding Rules\\n\\nThese rules apply to every file we create.\\n\\n- Routes only handle HTTP requests.\\n- Services contain business logic.\\n- Models only define database entities.\\n- Utility functions stay in `utils/`.\\n- Configuration never contains hardcoded secrets.\\n- Environment variables go into `.env`.\\n- Follow PEP 8.\\n- Use docstrings for public classes and functions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 📦 What We'll Build Next\\n\\nNow that the architecture is locked, the next deliverable is the **actual Flask project skeleton** with:\\n\\n- All folders created.\\n- Starter files in place.\\n- Configuration wired together.\\n- Database initialized.\\n- First page (`/`) running.\\n- Bootstrap integrated.\\n- Base template ready.\\n\\nOnce that's working, we'll move to **Sprint 1.2 – Authentication**, where users will be able to register, log in, and access the dashboard.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## One change I'd like to make before writing code\\n\\nInstead of creating the project as a collection of files, I want to generate it as a **professional repository** from day one.\\n\\nThat means every commit and folder will reflect a real development workflow. By the time we're finished, you'll have:\\n\\n- A clean Git repository.\\n- A complete Flask application.\\n- Documentation that matches the code.\\n- Milestone ZIP packages.\\n- A project that you can continue developing after college without needing to reorganize the codebase.\\n\\nI believe this is the best path because it serves both of your goals: earning full marks now and giving you a solid foundation for a future product.\",{},{\"_255\":1117,\"_262\":1147,\"_35\":1148,\"_37\":1149,\"_266\":1150,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1151,\"_275\":276},\"0e4cb0e3-97ef-454a-a27d-07beadc55d7d\",[1095],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1156},1785528135.572,1785528147.980143,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1154},{\"_632\":1152,\"_296\":1130,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1131,\"_302\":1131,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1153},[],[1155],\"ok do this \",{},{\"_255\":1145,\"_262\":1160,\"_35\":1161,\"_37\":1162,\"_266\":1163,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1164,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"1bfbb72d-5a31-479d-8f98-24ba08f10ae0\",[1117],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1195},1785527975.746518,1785527992.3545,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1193},{\"_279\":1165,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1166,\"_284\":1167,\"_286\":1168,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1169,\"_294\":1170,\"_296\":1171,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1172,\"_302\":1172,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1158,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1192},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1173,\"_581\":1174,\"_583\":1175,\"_585\":1176,\"_587\":1177,\"_589\":1178,\"_591\":1179,\"_593\":1180,\"_1181\":1182},[],\"778a2f63-ed6f-4387-af9e-c2cbb71edfb0\",\"e26a262d-2810-4d9b-a0b8-29d562b44a4e\",{\"_255\":1191,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1190,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1189,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1188,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1187,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1186,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1185,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1184,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"8\",{\"_255\":1183,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"2lozum\",\"nzd79i\",\"o28m2m\",\"cojmax\",\"4ehij0\",\"2jpvso\",\"fppnu2\",\"7cu13s\",\"47ne0r\",[316],[1194],\"Perfect. Now the real engineering starts.\\n\\nFrom this point on, we're no longer planning—we're **building**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🚀 Sprint 1 — Project Foundation\\n\\n**Objective:** Create a professional, scalable Flask project that serves as the foundation for the entire application.\\n\\nWe'll complete Sprint 1 before adding any features.\\n\\n## Sprint 1 Checklist\\n\\n```text\\nSprint 1 - Foundation\\n\\n□ Project Folder Structure\\n□ Python Virtual Environment\\n□ Git Repository\\n□ Requirements.txt\\n□ Flask Application Factory\\n□ Configuration Management\\n□ Environment Variables\\n□ Blueprint Architecture\\n□ SQLAlchemy Integration\\n□ MySQL Connection\\n□ Database Migration Setup\\n□ Logging System\\n□ Error Handling\\n□ Base HTML Template\\n□ Static Folder Structure\\n□ Authentication Blueprint\\n```\\n\\nNo shortcuts.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 1 — Project Structure\\n\\nThis is one place where I want to do things differently from most Flask tutorials.\\n\\nMost tutorials end up with a structure like this:\\n\\n```text\\napp.py\\ntemplates/\\nstatic/\\nmodels.py\\n```\\n\\nThat becomes difficult to maintain as the project grows.\\n\\nInstead, we'll use a modular architecture.\\n\\n```text\\nFinPilotAI/\\n│\\n├── app/\\n│   ├── __init__.py\\n│   ├── config.py\\n│   │\\n│   ├── auth/\\n│   │   ├── routes.py\\n│   │   ├── forms.py\\n│   │   ├── services.py\\n│   │   └── __init__.py\\n│   │\\n│   ├── dashboard/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── documents/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── ai/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── reports/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── chat/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── models/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── utils/\\n│   │\\n│   ├── templates/\\n│   │\\n│   └── static/\\n│\\n├── migrations/\\n│\\n├── instance/\\n│\\n├── tests/\\n│\\n├── uploads/\\n│\\n├── logs/\\n│\\n├── docs/\\n│\\n├── requirements.txt\\n│\\n├── run.py\\n│\\n├── .env\\n│\\n├── .gitignore\\n│\\n└── README.md\\n```\\n\\nThis is scalable enough for both your college project and a future product.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 2 — Why This Structure?\\n\\nEvery folder has one responsibility.\\n\\n| Folder | Purpose |\\n|---------|----------|\\n| auth | Login, registration, sessions |\\n| dashboard | Dashboard routes and logic |\\n| documents | Uploading, viewing, deleting files |\\n| ai | OCR, LLM, business insights |\\n| reports | PDF/Excel/CSV generation |\\n| chat | AI conversation |\\n| models | SQLAlchemy models |\\n| utils | Shared helper functions |\\n| templates | Jinja2 HTML templates |\\n| static | CSS, JS, images, fonts |\\n| uploads | User-uploaded documents |\\n| migrations | Database migrations |\\n| tests | Unit and integration tests |\\n| docs | Internal documentation |\\n| logs | Application logs |\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 3 — Technology Stack\\n\\nWe'll lock this now so the whole project stays consistent.\\n\\n| Layer | Technology |\\n|--------|------------|\\n| Backend | Flask 3.x |\\n| ORM | SQLAlchemy |\\n| Migrations | Flask-Migrate |\\n| Authentication | Flask-Login |\\n| Forms | Flask-WTF |\\n| Database | MySQL 8 |\\n| OCR | Tesseract OCR |\\n| AI | OpenAI-compatible API |\\n| Frontend | HTML5 + Bootstrap 5 + Jinja2 |\\n| Charts | Chart.js |\\n| Icons | Bootstrap Icons |\\n| File Upload | Flask + Werkzeug |\\n| Environment | python-dotenv |\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 4 — Python Packages\\n\\nOur initial `requirements.txt` will include:\\n\\n```text\\nFlask\\nFlask-SQLAlchemy\\nFlask-Migrate\\nFlask-Login\\nFlask-WTF\\nFlask-Mail\\npython-dotenv\\nmysqlclient\\nWerkzeug\\nWTForms\\nemail-validator\\nPillow\\npytesseract\\npdf2image\\nPyPDF2\\nopenai\\nrequests\\ngunicorn\\n```\\n\\nWe'll add packages only when we actually need them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 5 — Architecture Pattern\\n\\nWe'll use the **Application Factory Pattern**.\\n\\nWhy?\\n\\nBecause it gives us:\\n\\n- Modular blueprints\\n- Easier testing\\n- Cleaner configuration\\n- Better scalability\\n- Production-ready structure\\n\\nThis is considered one of the best practices for medium to large Flask applications.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 6 — Blueprint Architecture\\n\\nEach feature becomes an independent module.\\n\\n```text\\napp/\\n│\\n├── auth/\\n├── dashboard/\\n├── documents/\\n├── ai/\\n├── reports/\\n└── chat/\\n```\\n\\nEach blueprint contains:\\n\\n```text\\nroutes.py\\nservices.py\\nforms.py\\n__init__.py\\n```\\n\\nLater, we can also add:\\n\\n```text\\nvalidators.py\\nschemas.py\\n```\\n\\nif needed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 7 — Coding Standards\\n\\nWe'll define these rules now and follow them throughout development.\\n\\n- One responsibility per module.\\n- Business logic stays in `services.py`.\\n- Routes only handle HTTP requests and responses.\\n- Database access goes through SQLAlchemy models.\\n- Configuration stays outside the codebase using `.env`.\\n- Use type hints where practical.\\n- Follow PEP 8 naming and formatting.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 8 — Development Workflow\\n\\nEvery feature will follow the same lifecycle:\\n\\n```text\\nRequirement\\n      ↓\\nDatabase\\n      ↓\\nModel\\n      ↓\\nService\\n      ↓\\nRoute\\n      ↓\\nTemplate\\n      ↓\\nTesting\\n```\\n\\nThat consistency makes the project easier to understand and maintain.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🛠️ Before We Write the First Line of Code\\n\\nThere is one decision I want to make because it affects **every file in the project**.\\n\\n## I recommend we use **Flask Blueprints + Service Layer + Repository-like organization**, not just Blueprints.\\n\\nThat means:\\n\\n```text\\ndocuments/\\n│\\n├── routes.py        # HTTP endpoints\\n├── services.py      # Business logic\\n├── models.py        # (or shared in app/models)\\n├── validators.py    # Input validation\\n├── utils.py         # Helper functions\\n```\\n\\nThis keeps responsibilities separate and prevents route files from becoming hundreds of lines long.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## My commitment\\n\\nI don't want to generate isolated snippets of code that you have to assemble yourself.\\n\\nWe're going to build this like a real production project:\\n\\n- Every file in the correct folder.\\n- Every import working.\\n- Every module connected.\\n- Every dependency documented.\\n- Every sprint ending with a runnable application.\\n\\nBy the end of Sprint 1, you'll be able to start the Flask server, connect to MySQL, and see the foundation of the application running before we implement the first business feature.\",{},{\"_255\":1158,\"_262\":1199,\"_35\":1200,\"_37\":1201,\"_266\":1202,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1203,\"_275\":276},\"546b1828-661b-47c6-b05d-fd871011915d\",[1145],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1208},1785527975.025,1785527992.806743,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1206},{\"_632\":1204,\"_296\":1171,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1172,\"_302\":1172,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1205},[],[1207],\"ok lets start\",{},{\"_255\":1197,\"_262\":1212,\"_35\":1213,\"_37\":1214,\"_266\":1215,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1216,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"770d1723-38bf-4ef0-86de-cac0e88d1c55\",[1158],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1240},1785527923.388947,1785527936.94827,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1238},{\"_279\":1217,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1218,\"_284\":1219,\"_286\":1220,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1221,\"_294\":1222,\"_296\":1223,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1224,\"_302\":1224,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1210,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1237},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1225,\"_581\":1226,\"_583\":1227,\"_585\":1228,\"_587\":1229,\"_589\":1230},[],\"cb4fb248-e0e7-4d99-a28c-e1c7200883c9\",\"fcc019f6-9cc4-43b4-ad75-d03a0d6d017c\",{\"_255\":1236,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1235,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1234,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1233,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1232,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1231,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"98194q\",\"4pxxz3\",\"ay8yhd\",\"3em5mw\",\"17oztc\",\"rsgdco\",[316],[1239],\"I actually think this is the right moment to separate the project into **two tracks**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🎓 Track 1 — College Project\\n\\nThis is what you'll submit for evaluation.\\n\\n```\\nFinPilot AI v1.0\\n\\n✔ Flask\\n✔ MySQL\\n✔ OCR\\n✔ AI Document Analysis\\n✔ AI Chat\\n✔ Dashboard\\n✔ Reports\\n✔ Responsive UI\\n```\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Score maximum marks.\\n- Finish within one week.\\n- Stable and easy to explain in a viva.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🚀 Track 2 — Startup Product (Separate)\\n\\nThis will **not** be part of the college project.\\n\\n```\\nProject Codename\\n\\nBusiness Operating System (BOS)\\n\\nAI for Small Businesses\\n```\\n\\nEverything after Version 1.0 will be planned under this project.\\n\\nDifferent roadmap.\\nDifferent PRD.\\nDifferent milestones.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 📄 Product Requirements Document (PRD)\\n\\nThis PRD is **not** for college. It's for the startup.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (Version 1.0)\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n**Working Name:**\\n\u003e FinPilot AI (Temporary)\\n\\n**Vision**\\n\\n\u003e Build an AI-powered Business Operating System that enables small businesses to digitize financial documents, understand their business through AI, and reduce manual bookkeeping.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Problem Statement\\n\\nMillions of small businesses still manage invoices, receipts, and expenses manually.\\n\\nCurrent problems:\\n\\n- Paper invoices get lost.\\n- Searching old bills is difficult.\\n- Expense analysis is manual.\\n- Business owners don't understand spending patterns.\\n- No centralized document repository.\\n- Existing ERP software is expensive and complex.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Target Users\\n\\n### Primary\\n\\n- Shop Owners\\n- Retail Stores\\n- Wholesalers\\n- Small Manufacturers\\n- Freelancers\\n- Chartered Accountants\\n\\n### Secondary\\n\\n- Students\\n- Startups\\n- NGOs\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Vision Statement\\n\\n\u003e Make AI-powered financial management accessible to every small business.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Mission\\n\\n\u003e Transform every invoice, receipt, and financial document into structured, searchable, and actionable business intelligence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 6. Success Metrics\\n\\n### First Release\\n\\n```\\n100 Users\\n\\n1000 Documents\\n\\n95% OCR Accuracy\\n\\n90% AI Extraction Accuracy\\n\\n\u003c3 Seconds Processing Time\\n\\n95% System Availability\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 7. Core Features\\n\\n## Authentication\\n\\n- Register\\n- Login\\n- Forgot Password\\n- Profile\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Document Management\\n\\n- Upload\\n- Preview\\n- Search\\n- Download\\n- Delete\\n\\n---\\n\\n## AI Engine\\n\\n- OCR\\n- Data Extraction\\n- Invoice Parsing\\n- Receipt Parsing\\n- AI Summary\\n- Business Insights\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Dashboard\\n\\n- Expense Graph\\n- Categories\\n- Monthly Spending\\n- Recent Documents\\n- AI Suggestions\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Reports\\n\\n- PDF\\n- Excel\\n- CSV\\n\\n---\\n\\n## AI Chat\\n\\nAsk questions like:\\n\\n```\\nHow much did I spend in July?\\n\\nWhich vendor received the most money?\\n\\nShow GST expenses.\\n\\nWhat are my biggest expenses?\\n\\nSummarize this invoice.\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 8. Non Goals\\n\\nVersion 1.0 will NOT include\\n\\n- GST Filing\\n- Inventory\\n- Payroll\\n- Banking\\n- Multi-company\\n- Mobile App\\n- Multi-user collaboration\\n\\nThese are intentionally postponed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 9. User Stories\\n\\n### Business Owner\\n\\n\u003e I want to upload invoices so I don't lose them.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Accountant\\n\\n\u003e I want AI to extract invoice information automatically.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Student\\n\\n\u003e I want to search old receipts instantly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Freelancer\\n\\n\u003e I want monthly expense reports.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 10. MVP Scope\\n\\n```\\nAuthentication\\n\\nDashboard\\n\\nUpload\\n\\nOCR\\n\\nAI Extraction\\n\\nReports\\n\\nAI Chat\\n\\nSearch\\n```\\n\\nNothing more.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 11. Tech Stack\\n\\nFrontend\\n\\n- HTML5\\n- CSS3\\n- Bootstrap 5\\n- JavaScript\\n\\nBackend\\n\\n- Flask\\n- SQLAlchemy\\n\\nDatabase\\n\\n- MySQL\\n\\nAI\\n\\n- OCR\\n- LLM API\\n\\nCharts\\n\\n- Chart.js\\n\\nAuthentication\\n\\n- Flask-Login\\n\\nFile Storage\\n\\n- Local Storage (MVP)\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 12. Future Roadmap\\n\\nVersion 2\\n\\n- Inventory\\n\\n- Sales\\n\\n- Vendors\\n\\n- Employees\\n\\n- Notifications\\n\\n---\\n\\nVersion 3\\n\\n- GST\\n\\n- OCR Improvements\\n\\n- AI Forecasting\\n\\n- Smart Alerts\\n\\n---\\n\\nVersion 4\\n\\n- Multi Company\\n\\n- Team Collaboration\\n\\n- Mobile App\\n\\n- API\\n\\n- Integrations\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 13. Risks\\n\\nTechnical\\n\\n- OCR quality.\\n- AI API cost.\\n- Large file uploads.\\n\\nBusiness\\n\\n- User adoption.\\n- Competition.\\n- Data privacy.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 14. Long-Term Vision\\n\\nBecome the operating system for small businesses by combining document intelligence, financial insights, and AI assistance in one platform.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🏗️ Now, Let's Build It Properly\\n\\nFrom this point onward, I suggest we stop writing documents for a while and start **building the actual application**.\\n\\nWe'll follow this sequence:\\n\\n```\\nSprint 1 – Project Setup\\n│\\n├── Flask Project Structure\\n├── Virtual Environment\\n├── Configuration\\n├── MySQL Database\\n├── SQLAlchemy\\n├── Authentication\\n└── Git Repository\\n\\nSprint 2 – Authentication Module\\n\\nSprint 3 – Dashboard\\n\\nSprint 4 – Document Upload\\n\\nSprint 5 – OCR Engine\\n\\nSprint 6 – AI Analysis\\n\\nSprint 7 – Reports\\n\\nSprint 8 – AI Chat\\n\\nSprint 9 – Testing \u0026 Deployment\\n```\\n\\n## My recommendation\\n\\nWe've done enough planning to start implementation confidently. The next step should be creating the **complete Flask project foundation**—the folder structure, configuration, dependencies, database connection, authentication blueprint, and development environment. Once that's in place, every new feature will plug into a clean architecture instead of being added ad hoc.\\n\\nWe'll build it like a real software product, one working sprint at a time, while continuing to generate the documentation, diagrams, and ZIP deliverables alongside the code.\",{},{\"_255\":1210,\"_262\":1244,\"_35\":1245,\"_266\":1246,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":331,\"_273\":1247,\"_275\":276},\"4f031b56-03f0-4937-8df5-626c908351ae\",[1197],{\"_322\":336,\"_273\":1249},1785527923.4089108,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1248},{\"_296\":1223,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1224,\"_302\":1224,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1242,\"_306\":10,\"_333\":26,\"_304\":14},[335],{},{\"_255\":1242,\"_262\":1253,\"_35\":1254,\"_266\":1255,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1256,\"_275\":276},\"bca4fb7d-3d48-4706-be78-0b35490e4d82\",[1210],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1257},1785527923.3902054,{\"_317\":517,\"_518\":335},{\"_300\":1224,\"_302\":1224,\"_305\":1251,\"_306\":10,\"_516\":26},{},{\"_255\":1251,\"_262\":1261,\"_35\":1262,\"_266\":1263,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1264,\"_275\":276},\"62ea8f8f-e2cf-43ab-88af-be2799a3dee7\",[1242],{\"_322\":336,\"_273\":1266},1785527923.23512,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1265},{\"_333\":26,\"_296\":1223,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1224,\"_302\":1224,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1259,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},[335],{},{\"_255\":1259,\"_262\":1270,\"_35\":1271,\"_37\":1272,\"_266\":1273,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1274,\"_275\":276},\"5401a0e0-b840-4794-aa21-bc7061297f32\",[1251],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1279},1785527922.66,1785527937.387981,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1277},{\"_632\":1275,\"_296\":1223,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1224,\"_302\":1224,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1276},[],[1278],\"ok make a prd but make it as the separate from college project and let start by building it\",{},{\"_255\":1268,\"_262\":1283,\"_35\":1284,\"_37\":1285,\"_266\":1286,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1287,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"4e7d956d-609c-4179-86cd-c717f1de2c55\",[1259],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1309},1785527798.162135,1785527807.218507,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1307},{\"_279\":1288,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1289,\"_284\":1290,\"_286\":1291,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1292,\"_294\":1293,\"_296\":1294,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1295,\"_302\":1295,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1281,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1306},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1296,\"_581\":1297,\"_583\":1298,\"_585\":1299,\"_587\":1300},[],\"c360701c-5afb-49ad-b1be-1fd00bbe822e\",\"35f08bf5-d9b3-410d-9b9f-a6889a4dd2d3\",{\"_255\":1305,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1304,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1303,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1302,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1301,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"morqaa\",\"2v2goo\",\"wg8sz6\",\"nsj201\",\"3ds7qq\",[316],[1308],\"Great. I think we're making one decision that will significantly improve the quality of your project.\\n\\n## We are **not building pages**.\\n\\nWe are **designing a product**.\\n\\nThat's a completely different mindset.\\n\\nMost college projects do this:\\n\\n```\\nLogin Page\\n↓\\n\\nDashboard\\n↓\\n\\nUpload\\n↓\\n\\nDone\\n```\\n\\nWe're doing this instead:\\n\\n```\\nBusiness Problem\\n        ↓\\nSoftware Architecture\\n        ↓\\nDatabase\\n        ↓\\nDesign System\\n        ↓\\nUI Components\\n        ↓\\nWireframes\\n        ↓\\nHigh-Fidelity UI\\n        ↓\\nBackend\\n        ↓\\nAI\\n        ↓\\nTesting\\n        ↓\\nDeployment\\n```\\n\\nThat's how real software companies work.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🏆 I want to make one more improvement\\n\\nNow that I know this project may become your startup later, I don't want to think like a college student anymore.\\n\\nI want to think like a **Product Manager**.\\n\\nSo before we write a single line of Flask code, I want to create one document that almost no final-year project includes.\\n\\n# Product Requirements Document (PRD)\\n\\nThink of it as the \\\"master document\\\" for the entire application.\\n\\nIt will include:\\n\\n```\\nProblem Statement\\n\\nTarget Users\\n\\nGoals\\n\\nUser Personas\\n\\nFeatures\\n\\nUser Stories\\n\\nSuccess Metrics\\n\\nConstraints\\n\\nRisks\\n\\nFuture Scope\\n```\\n\\nThis document becomes the reference for every future decision.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Then we'll create a Project Bible\\n\\nThis will be our internal guide.\\n\\n```\\nFinPilot AI\\n\\n│\\n\\n├── Product Vision\\n\\n├── Coding Standards\\n\\n├── Folder Structure\\n\\n├── Database Rules\\n\\n├── API Rules\\n\\n├── Naming Convention\\n\\n├── Git Workflow\\n\\n├── UI Standards\\n\\n├── Documentation Standards\\n```\\n\\nWhenever we make a decision, we check the Project Bible first.\\n\\nNo inconsistencies.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# The Development Process\\n\\nThis is exactly how we'll build the project.\\n\\n```\\nSprint 1\\nProject Foundation\\n\\n✔ PRD\\n✔ SRS\\n✔ Architecture\\n✔ Database\\n✔ UI\\n\\n----------------------------\\n\\nSprint 2\\n\\nBackend\\n\\nAuthentication\\n\\nDatabase\\n\\nUpload\\n\\nOCR\\n\\nAI\\n\\n----------------------------\\n\\nSprint 3\\n\\nFrontend\\n\\nDashboard\\n\\nReports\\n\\nDocuments\\n\\nChat\\n\\n----------------------------\\n\\nSprint 4\\n\\nTesting\\n\\nOptimization\\n\\nDeployment\\n\\nDocumentation\\n\\nPresentation\\n\\nZIP Package\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🚀 One more thing that I want to add (this is where our project becomes unique)\\n\\nI don't want our project to be called just an **AI Invoice Scanner**.\\n\\nI want it to become an **AI Business Operating System**.\\n\\nVersion 1.0 (College Project) will include:\\n\\n- AI Invoice Scanner\\n- Receipt Scanner\\n- AI Business Dashboard\\n- AI Reports\\n- AI Chat\\n\\nLater, Version 2.0 can evolve into:\\n\\n- Inventory Management\\n- Expense Tracking\\n- Employee Management\\n- GST Analytics\\n- Sales Dashboard\\n- Business Forecasting\\n- Smart Notifications\\n- Multi-user Collaboration\\n\\nNotice what's happening?\\n\\nWe're **not changing the college project**.\\n\\nWe're designing Version 1.0 in a way that naturally grows into a much larger product without requiring a redesign.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📌 From this point onward, I have one commitment for this project\\n\\nI will not take shortcuts.\\n\\nEvery diagram, every database table, every Flask model, every API, every HTML page, every CSS component, every JavaScript file, every AI prompt, every SQL query, and every document will be designed so that:\\n\\n1. **You can confidently explain it during your viva.**\\n2. **It follows sound software engineering practices.**\\n3. **It can be extended into a real commercial SaaS after Version 1.0.**\\n\\nWe'll build it incrementally, with each sprint ending in a working, documented milestone and an updated ZIP package containing everything completed so far. By the end, you won't just have a final-year project—you'll have the foundation of a real software product.\",{},{\"_255\":1281,\"_262\":1313,\"_35\":1314,\"_266\":1315,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":331,\"_273\":1316,\"_275\":276},\"7a151336-c13b-4b86-bce1-609efa1c88ab\",[1268],{\"_322\":336,\"_273\":1318},1785527798.0738719,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1317},{\"_347\":26,\"_296\":1294,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1295,\"_302\":1295,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1311,\"_306\":10,\"_333\":26,\"_304\":14},[335],{},{\"_255\":1311,\"_262\":1322,\"_35\":1323,\"_37\":1324,\"_266\":1325,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1326,\"_275\":276},\"5efe8af5-d42e-43b3-9967-b25bdc655988\",[1281],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1331},1785527797.226,1785527807.303771,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1329},{\"_632\":1327,\"_296\":1294,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1295,\"_302\":1295,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1328},[],[1330],\"ok it is nice\",{},{\"_255\":1320,\"_262\":1335,\"_35\":1336,\"_37\":1337,\"_266\":1338,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1339,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"62bc3ac6-103d-48f3-b533-ac4c9c2b112e\",[1311],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1402},1785527509.298752,1785527524.377339,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1400},{\"_279\":1340,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1341,\"_284\":1342,\"_286\":1343,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1344,\"_294\":1345,\"_296\":1346,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1347,\"_302\":1347,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1333,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1399},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1348,\"_581\":1349,\"_583\":1350,\"_585\":1351,\"_587\":1352,\"_589\":1353,\"_591\":1354,\"_593\":1355,\"_1181\":1356,\"_1357\":1358,\"_1359\":1360,\"_1361\":1362,\"_1363\":1364,\"_1365\":1366,\"_1367\":1368,\"_1369\":1370,\"_1371\":1372,\"_1373\":1374,\"_1375\":1376,\"_1377\":1378},[],\"c301f06f-4f92-4398-a51e-bfb5f9b27ef2\",\"f36f128a-9845-4547-858d-5481715f88a4\",{\"_255\":1398,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1397,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1396,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1395,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1394,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1393,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1392,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1391,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1390,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"9\",{\"_255\":1389,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"10\",{\"_255\":1388,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"11\",{\"_255\":1387,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"12\",{\"_255\":1386,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"13\",{\"_255\":1385,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"14\",{\"_255\":1384,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"15\",{\"_255\":1383,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"16\",{\"_255\":1382,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"17\",{\"_255\":1381,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"18\",{\"_255\":1380,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"19\",{\"_255\":1379,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"yo14ff\",\"n811cu\",\"27r0g4\",\"1fv235\",\"umbq1j\",\"ywt42b\",\"apg9jh\",\"9cm5fe\",\"4rlkck\",\"6zjnzu\",\"cfcq6f\",\"uptu0p\",\"62oe3z\",\"7hth00\",\"crsm6j\",\"mo0s7p\",\"smhi8f\",\"k6ojcw\",\"gf9fem\",\"9gau2o\",[316],[1401],\"Perfect. Now we're entering the phase that I think will make your project stand out the most.\\n\\n\u003e **A professor usually forms an opinion about a project within the first 30 seconds.**\\n\u003e\\n\u003e If they see a modern, professional interface, they'll immediately perceive it as a higher-quality project.\\n\\nThis is why I don't want to build the UI page by page. I want to build a **Design System** first—the same approach used by companies like Google (Material Design), Microsoft (Fluent UI), and Atlassian.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🎨 PHASE 2.5 — UI/UX SYSTEM DESIGN\\n\\n## Development Flow\\n\\n```text\\nDesign System\\n      ↓\\nComponent Library\\n      ↓\\nWireframes\\n      ↓\\nHigh-Fidelity UI\\n      ↓\\nHTML Templates\\n      ↓\\nFlask Integration\\n```\\n\\nEverything starts with the Design System.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 1 — Product Personality\\n\\nBefore choosing colors or fonts, define what the application should feel like.\\n\\n## Keywords\\n\\n```text\\nProfessional\\n\\nModern\\n\\nMinimal\\n\\nTrustworthy\\n\\nFast\\n\\nAI-Powered\\n\\nFinancial\\n\\nPremium\\n```\\n\\nIf someone opens the application, they should think:\\n\\n\u003e \\\"This looks like a real SaaS product.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 2 — UI Style\\n\\nWe'll avoid outdated Bootstrap admin templates.\\n\\nInstead, we'll combine ideas from:\\n\\n- Stripe Dashboard\\n- Notion\\n- GitHub\\n- Linear\\n- Vercel\\n- Figma\\n\\nCharacteristics:\\n\\n- Clean spacing\\n- Rounded cards\\n- Soft shadows\\n- Simple icons\\n- Lots of white space\\n- Professional typography\\n- Responsive layout\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 3 — Color System\\n\\n## Primary\\n\\n```text\\nBlue 600\\n\\n#2563EB\\n```\\n\\nRepresents trust, technology, and finance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Success\\n\\n```text\\n#10B981\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Warning\\n\\n```text\\n#F59E0B\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Danger\\n\\n```text\\n#EF4444\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Background\\n\\n```text\\n#F8FAFC\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Surface\\n\\n```text\\n#FFFFFF\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Text\\n\\n```text\\nPrimary\\n\\n#0F172A\\n\\nSecondary\\n\\n#475569\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 4 — Typography\\n\\nFont\\n\\n\u003e Inter\\n\\nSizes\\n\\n```text\\nH1 36\\n\\nH2 30\\n\\nH3 24\\n\\nBody 16\\n\\nSmall 14\\n\\nCaption 12\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 5 — Spacing System\\n\\nWe'll use an 8-point spacing system.\\n\\n```text\\n4px\\n\\n8px\\n\\n16px\\n\\n24px\\n\\n32px\\n\\n48px\\n\\n64px\\n```\\n\\nEverything aligns perfectly.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 6 — Border Radius\\n\\n```text\\nButtons\\n\\n10px\\n\\nCards\\n\\n16px\\n\\nInputs\\n\\n12px\\n\\nDialogs\\n\\n20px\\n```\\n\\nRounded but professional.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 7 — Shadows\\n\\nWe'll use only three shadow levels.\\n\\nSmall\\n\\nCards\\n\\nMedium\\n\\nDropdowns\\n\\nLarge\\n\\nDialogs\\n\\nNo heavy shadows.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 8 — Icons\\n\\nWe'll use a single icon library throughout the application.\\n\\nRecommended:\\n\\n- Bootstrap Icons\\n\\nor\\n\\n- Lucide Icons\\n\\nNo mixing icon sets.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 9 — Layout\\n\\nEvery page follows the same structure.\\n\\n```text\\n+-------------------------------------------+\\n| Navbar                                    |\\n+----------+--------------------------------+\\n| Sidebar  | Main Content                   |\\n|          |                                |\\n|          | Dashboard Cards                |\\n|          |                                |\\n|          | Charts                         |\\n|          |                                |\\n|          | Tables                         |\\n|          |                                |\\n+----------+--------------------------------+\\n```\\n\\nConsistency reduces development effort.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 10 — Pages\\n\\nWe'll design these screens.\\n\\n```text\\nAuthentication\\n\\nLogin\\n\\nRegister\\n\\nForgot Password\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nDashboard\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nUpload Documents\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nDocument List\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nDocument Details\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nAI Analysis\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nAI Chat\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nReports\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nProfile\\n\\n--------------------------------\\n\\nSettings\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 11 — Dashboard Layout\\n\\nThis is the application's main screen.\\n\\n```text\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n\\nNavbar\\n\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n\\nSidebar\\n\\nDashboard\\n\\nUpload\\n\\nDocuments\\n\\nReports\\n\\nAI Chat\\n\\nSettings\\n\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n\\nTop Cards\\n\\nTotal Documents\\n\\nTotal Expenses\\n\\nCategories\\n\\nMonthly Spending\\n\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n\\nCharts\\n\\nExpense Trend\\n\\nCategory Distribution\\n\\nVendor Analysis\\n\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n\\nRecent Documents\\n\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n\\nAI Insights\\n\\n----------------------------------------------------\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 12 — Upload Screen\\n\\n```text\\n----------------------------------\\n\\nUpload Card\\n\\nDrag \u0026 Drop Area\\n\\nBrowse Button\\n\\nSupported Formats\\n\\nRecent Uploads\\n\\n----------------------------------\\n```\\n\\nUsers should be able to drag files directly onto the page.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 13 — AI Analysis Screen\\n\\nThis is the feature that will impress your evaluators.\\n\\n```text\\n---------------------------------------\\n\\nInvoice Preview\\n\\n-------------------------\\n\\nVendor\\n\\nAmount\\n\\nGST\\n\\nDate\\n\\nInvoice Number\\n\\nCategory\\n\\nConfidence Score\\n\\nAI Summary\\n\\nBusiness Insights\\n\\n---------------------------------------\\n```\\n\\nInstead of showing raw OCR text, we show structured information with confidence and AI-generated insights.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 14 — AI Chat\\n\\n```text\\n+-------------------------------------+\\n\\nChat Window\\n\\n-------------------------------------\\n\\nYou\\n\\nHow much did I spend this month?\\n\\nAI\\n\\n₹48,540\\n\\nMost expenses were office supplies.\\n\\n-------------------------------------\\n\\nInput Box\\n\\nSend Button\\n\\n+-------------------------------------+\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 15 — Reports\\n\\n```text\\nMonthly Report\\n\\nExpense Report\\n\\nVendor Report\\n\\nExport PDF\\n\\nExport Excel\\n\\nExport CSV\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 📁 UI Deliverables\\n\\nThe UI package will eventually contain:\\n\\n```text\\n05_UI/\\n\\nDesign_System.pdf\\n\\nColor_Guide.pdf\\n\\nTypography.pdf\\n\\nComponent_Library.pdf\\n\\nWireframes.pdf\\n\\nHigh_Fidelity_Screens/\\n\\nLogin.png\\n\\nRegister.png\\n\\nDashboard.png\\n\\nUpload.png\\n\\nDocuments.png\\n\\nAnalysis.png\\n\\nReports.png\\n\\nChat.png\\n\\nProfile.png\\n\\nSettings.png\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 💡 One Major Improvement Before We Build the UI\\n\\nI don't want to use plain Bootstrap components everywhere.\\n\\nInstead, we'll build our own small **component library**:\\n\\n### Buttons\\n- Primary\\n- Secondary\\n- Success\\n- Danger\\n- Outline\\n\\n### Cards\\n- Statistics Card\\n- Document Card\\n- AI Insight Card\\n\\n### Tables\\n- Searchable\\n- Sortable\\n- Responsive\\n\\n### Forms\\n- Floating labels\\n- Validation states\\n- File upload component\\n\\n### Modals\\n- Delete confirmation\\n- AI processing status\\n- Report generation\\n\\nThis approach has two big advantages:\\n\\n1. **Professional consistency**: every page looks like part of the same product.\\n2. **Faster development**: once components are built, every new page becomes much easier to assemble.\\n\\n## My recommendation\\n\\nBefore we create any HTML, let's spend one sprint designing **the Dashboard**. It is the heart of the application and sets the visual language for every other screen. Once the dashboard is finalized, the remaining pages will naturally follow the same design system, making the entire project cohesive and much easier to implement.\",{},{\"_255\":1333,\"_262\":1406,\"_35\":1407,\"_37\":1408,\"_266\":1409,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1410,\"_275\":276},\"5db6e910-ea1c-4f9c-bcd8-9b945db6070a\",[1320],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1415},1785527508.912,1785527524.376161,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1413},{\"_632\":1411,\"_296\":1346,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1347,\"_302\":1347,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1412},[],[1414],\"so let start\",{},{\"_255\":1404,\"_262\":1419,\"_35\":1420,\"_37\":1421,\"_266\":1422,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1423,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"a1e6dadf-f587-494e-a5d9-a67c4a54dcd7\",[1333],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1437},1785527042.007558,1785527052.391655,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1435},{\"_279\":1424,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1425,\"_284\":1426,\"_286\":1427,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1428,\"_294\":1429,\"_296\":1430,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1431,\"_302\":1431,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1417,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1434},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1432},[],\"b730fef2-7b2a-40f7-ba8e-ee7a3d449705\",\"c86aa053-ac40-47cf-b596-069b04d13c82\",{\"_255\":1433,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"pds2jg\",[316],[1436],\"Done! I've created the initial **Database Design Pack (v2)** for the project.\\n\\n### 📦 Download\\n[**FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v2_Database.zip**](sandbox:/mnt/data/FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v2_Database.zip)\\n\\n### Included\\n\\n```text\\n05_Database/\\n├── ER_Diagram.png\\n├── Database_Schema.png\\n├── Data_Dictionary.pdf\\n└── SQL_Schema.sql\\n```\\n\\n### Important Note\\n\\nThis is the **first engineering draft**, not the final version.\\n\\nAs we continue, I want to replace these simple diagrams with **professional-grade deliverables** that look like they were produced by an enterprise architecture team. The final package will include:\\n\\n- Fully attributed ER diagrams (showing every field, PK, FK, data type, nullability).\\n- Crow's Foot notation.\\n- Normalization documentation (1NF, 2NF, 3NF).\\n- Index strategy.\\n- Constraints and relationships.\\n- SQL scripts that run directly in MySQL.\\n- SQLAlchemy model mapping.\\n- Database migration plan.\\n- Database dictionary with every column documented.\\n- High-resolution PNG, SVG, PDF, and editable source files where applicable.\\n\\nThese final versions will replace the draft files in the milestone ZIP, so you won't end up with duplicate or inconsistent documentation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Next Major Milestone\\n\\nNow we begin one of the most important parts of the project:\\n\\n### 🎨 UI/UX System Design\\n\\nThis is where we'll design:\\n\\n- Login Page\\n- Register Page\\n- Dashboard\\n- Upload Documents\\n- Document Details\\n- AI Analysis View\\n- AI Chat\\n- Reports\\n- Profile\\n- Settings\\n\\nUnlike typical college projects, we'll first build a **design system** (colors, typography, spacing, reusable components) and then create all screens from it. That way the entire application has a consistent, professional appearance and is much easier to implement in Flask. This UI will be one of the strongest differentiators of your project.\",{},{\"_255\":1417,\"_262\":1441,\"_35\":1442,\"_37\":1443,\"_266\":1444,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1445,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":405},\"f3a665a8-2b86-4937-b955-e16bd0a36594\",[1404],{\"_322\":455,\"_440\":456,\"_273\":1466},1785527040.334701,1785527041.709382,{\"_317\":454,\"_318\":1460},{\"_281\":26,\"_406\":1446,\"_296\":1430,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1431,\"_302\":1431,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1439,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_268\":408,\"_409\":1447,\"_411\":1442,\"_37\":1443,\"_412\":1448,\"_414\":1443,\"_415\":-5,\"_416\":-5,\"_417\":-5,\"_418\":1449,\"_420\":1450,\"_422\":-5},\"1a6c5a4a-65a2-4e4e-b6d7-f758e6a0c033\",\"from graphviz import Digraph\\nfrom reportlab.platypus import SimpleDocTemplate, Table, TableStyle, Paragraph\\nfrom reportlab.lib import colors\\nfrom reportlab.lib.styles import getSampleStyleSheet\\nimport os, zipfile\\n\\nbase=\\\"/mnt/data/FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v2/05_Database\\\"\\nos.makedirs(base,exist_ok=True)\\nstyles=getSampleStyleSheet()\\n\\n# ER diagram\\ng=Digraph(\\\"ER\\\",format=\\\"png\\\")\\ng.attr(rankdir=\\\"LR\\\")\\nents=[\\\"users\\\",\\\"documents\\\",\\\"document_analysis\\\",\\\"reports\\\",\\\"chat_history\\\"]\\nfor e in ents:\\n    g.node(e,e,shape=\\\"record\\\")\\ng.edge(\\\"users\\\",\\\"documents\\\",label=\\\"1:N\\\")\\ng.edge(\\\"documents\\\",\\\"document_analysis\\\",label=\\\"1:1\\\")\\ng.edge(\\\"users\\\",\\\"reports\\\",label=\\\"1:N\\\")\\ng.edge(\\\"users\\\",\\\"chat_history\\\",label=\\\"1:N\\\")\\ng.render(os.path.join(base,\\\"ER_Diagram\\\"),cleanup=True)\\n\\nschema=Digraph(\\\"Schema\\\",format=\\\"png\\\")\\nschema.attr(rankdir=\\\"TB\\\")\\nschema.node(\\\"u\\\",\\\"users\\\\nid\\\\nfull_name\\\\nemail\\\")\\nschema.node(\\\"d\\\",\\\"documents\\\\nid\\\\nuser_id\\\\nstored_filename\\\")\\nschema.node(\\\"a\\\",\\\"document_analysis\\\\ndocument_id\\\\nvendor_name\\\\ntotal_amount\\\")\\nschema.node(\\\"r\\\",\\\"reports\\\\nuser_id\\\")\\nschema.node(\\\"c\\\",\\\"chat_history\\\\nuser_id\\\")\\nschema.edges([(\\\"u\\\",\\\"d\\\"),(\\\"d\\\",\\\"a\\\"),(\\\"u\\\",\\\"r\\\"),(\\\"u\\\",\\\"c\\\")])\\nschema.render(os.path.join(base,\\\"Database_Schema\\\"),cleanup=True)\\n\\nsql=\\\"\\\"\\\"CREATE TABLE users (...);\\nCREATE TABLE documents (... user_id BIGINT ...);\\nCREATE TABLE document_analysis (... document_id BIGINT UNIQUE ...);\\nCREATE TABLE reports (... user_id BIGINT ...);\\nCREATE TABLE chat_history (... user_id BIGINT ...);\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nopen(os.path.join(base,\\\"SQL_Schema.sql\\\"),\\\"w\\\").write(sql)\\n\\ndoc=SimpleDocTemplate(os.path.join(base,\\\"Data_Dictionary.pdf\\\"))\\ndata=[[\\\"Table\\\",\\\"Purpose\\\"],\\n[\\\"users\\\",\\\"Authentication/profile\\\"],\\n[\\\"documents\\\",\\\"Uploaded files\\\"],\\n[\\\"document_analysis\\\",\\\"AI extracted structured data\\\"],\\n[\\\"reports\\\",\\\"Generated reports\\\"],\\n[\\\"chat_history\\\",\\\"AI conversations\\\"]]\\nt=Table(data)\\nt.setStyle(TableStyle([(\\\"GRID\\\",(0,0),(-1,-1),1,colors.black),(\\\"BACKGROUND\\\",(0,0),(-1,0),colors.lightblue)]))\\ndoc.build([Paragraph(\\\"Data Dictionary\\\",styles[\\\"Heading1\\\"]),t])\\n\\nzip_path=\\\"/mnt/data/FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v2_Database.zip\\\"\\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(zip_path,\\\"w\\\") as z:\\n    for r,_,fs in os.walk(\\\"/mnt/data/FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v2\\\"):\\n        for f in fs:\\n            p=os.path.join(r,f)\\n            z.write(p,os.path.relpath(p,\\\"/mnt/data/FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v2\\\"))\\nprint(zip_path)\\n\",[1464],[1451,1452,1453,1454],{\"_427\":268,\"_428\":1462,\"_266\":1463},{\"_427\":443,\"_428\":1461},{\"_427\":437,\"_428\":1458,\"_266\":1459},{\"_427\":268,\"_428\":1455,\"_266\":1456},{\"_433\":1457,\"_435\":436},{\"_431\":432},\"82368727-da296828e99f646e793fdc23_217_8\",{\"_433\":1457,\"_435\":436},{\"_440\":441,\"_318\":1460},\"/mnt/data/FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v2_Database.zip\\n\",{\"_433\":1457,\"_435\":436},{\"_433\":1457,\"_435\":436},{\"_431\":447},{\"_298\":437,\"_449\":1465,\"_451\":441,\"_452\":453,\"_318\":1460},1785527041.4429991,{},{\"_255\":1439,\"_262\":1470,\"_35\":1471,\"_266\":1472,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":14,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1473,\"_275\":456,\"_277\":405},\"b7a7c166-09aa-49ed-97e8-ab024eadbb20\",[1417],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1479},1785527032.44029,{\"_317\":412,\"_470\":471,\"_318\":1448},{\"_279\":1474,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1475,\"_284\":1476,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_296\":1430,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1431,\"_302\":1431,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_305\":1477,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1478},[],[],\"8b028cb8-6801-4a92-8e16-f21a81570c71\",[469],{},{\"_255\":1468,\"_262\":1483,\"_35\":1484,\"_37\":1485,\"_266\":1486,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1487,\"_275\":276},\"1f79e6ee-2ff5-41d4-91bb-d116bfb8ed30\",[1439],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1492},1785527032.053,1785527052.883887,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1490},{\"_632\":1488,\"_296\":1430,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1431,\"_302\":1431,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1489},[],[1491],\"ok create it \",{},{\"_255\":1481,\"_262\":1496,\"_35\":1497,\"_37\":1498,\"_266\":1499,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1500,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"62b2a436-da32-4f57-9a30-447931711fb6\",[1468],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1534},1785527001.423791,1785527016.79112,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1532},{\"_279\":1501,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1502,\"_284\":1503,\"_286\":1504,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1505,\"_294\":1506,\"_296\":1507,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1508,\"_302\":1508,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1494,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1531},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1509,\"_581\":1510,\"_583\":1511,\"_585\":1512,\"_587\":1513,\"_589\":1514,\"_591\":1515,\"_593\":1516,\"_1181\":1517,\"_1357\":1518,\"_1359\":1519},[],\"7424b7f6-ec0a-4e02-8063-3f7f24433286\",\"58a2bd71-f5e2-4e5f-be3c-babde28db30f\",{\"_255\":1530,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1529,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1528,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1527,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1526,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1525,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1524,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1523,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1522,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1521,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1520,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"k0ji69\",\"f4x274\",\"xockrs\",\"hgb8yv\",\"8lsci4\",\"z8ibbr\",\"c9x3sz\",\"dbszre\",\"d9rhaa\",\"ccq9oq\",\"81d04c\",[316],[1533],\"Excellent. Then it's decided.\\n\\nFrom now on, the table will be named **`document_analysis`** instead of `extracted_data`. This is one of those architectural decisions that will save us from redesigning the database when we move to the enterprise version.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🚀 Database Design Sprint Begins\\n\\nNow we're going to design the database like professional backend engineers.\\n\\n## Database Design Process\\n\\n```text\\nBusiness Rules\\n      ↓\\nEntities\\n      ↓\\nAttributes\\n      ↓\\nRelationships\\n      ↓\\nNormalization\\n      ↓\\nER Diagram\\n      ↓\\nSQL Schema\\n      ↓\\nFlask Models\\n```\\n\\nEverything else in the project depends on this.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 1 — Business Rules\\n\\nEvery database is built around business rules.\\n\\n## Rule 1\\n\\nA user can own multiple documents.\\n\\n```text\\n1 User\\n↓\\n\\nMany Documents\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rule 2\\n\\nEach uploaded document generates exactly one analysis record.\\n\\n```text\\n1 Document\\n↓\\n\\n1 Document Analysis\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rule 3\\n\\nA user can generate multiple reports.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rule 4\\n\\nA user can have multiple AI conversations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rule 5\\n\\nA document always belongs to exactly one user.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rule 6\\n\\nEvery analysis record belongs to exactly one document.\\n\\nThese rules define our relationships before we create any tables.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 2 — Database Entities\\n\\nOur Version 1.0 database will contain five core entities.\\n\\n## 1. users\\n\\nStores authentication and profile information.\\n\\nKey attributes:\\n- id\\n- full_name\\n- email\\n- password_hash\\n- company_name\\n- created_at\\n- updated_at\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. documents\\n\\nStores uploaded files.\\n\\nKey attributes:\\n- id\\n- user_id\\n- original_filename\\n- stored_filename\\n- file_type\\n- file_size\\n- upload_status\\n- uploaded_at\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. document_analysis\\n\\nStores AI results.\\n\\nKey attributes:\\n- id\\n- document_id\\n- vendor_name\\n- invoice_number\\n- transaction_date\\n- subtotal\\n- gst_amount\\n- total_amount\\n- payment_method\\n- category\\n- ai_summary\\n- created_at\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. reports\\n\\nStores generated reports.\\n\\nKey attributes:\\n- id\\n- user_id\\n- report_name\\n- report_type\\n- file_path\\n- generated_at\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. chat_history\\n\\nStores AI conversations.\\n\\nKey attributes:\\n- id\\n- user_id\\n- question\\n- answer\\n- created_at\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 3 — Relationships\\n\\n```text\\nusers\\n │\\n ├──────────────┐\\n │              │\\n ▼              ▼\\n\\ndocuments    chat_history\\n │\\n ▼\\n\\ndocument_analysis\\n\\nusers\\n │\\n ▼\\n\\nreports\\n```\\n\\nRelationship summary:\\n\\n| Parent | Child | Relationship |\\n|---------|-------|--------------|\\n| users | documents | 1 : Many |\\n| users | reports | 1 : Many |\\n| users | chat_history | 1 : Many |\\n| documents | document_analysis | 1 : 1 |\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 4 — Primary Keys\\n\\nEvery table uses:\\n\\n```sql\\nid BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY\\n```\\n\\nWhy BIGINT?\\n\\n- Better long-term scalability.\\n- Standard in many production systems.\\n- No schema changes if the project grows.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 5 — Foreign Keys\\n\\n```text\\ndocuments.user_id\\n      ↓\\nusers.id\\n\\ndocument_analysis.document_id\\n      ↓\\ndocuments.id\\n\\nreports.user_id\\n      ↓\\nusers.id\\n\\nchat_history.user_id\\n      ↓\\nusers.id\\n```\\n\\nWe'll also enforce referential integrity using foreign key constraints.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 6 — Constraints\\n\\nWe'll define constraints from the beginning:\\n\\n### users\\n- email → UNIQUE\\n- full_name → NOT NULL\\n- password_hash → NOT NULL\\n\\n### documents\\n- user_id → NOT NULL\\n- stored_filename → UNIQUE\\n- upload_status → Default: `\\\"processed\\\"`\\n\\n### document_analysis\\n- document_id → UNIQUE\\n- total_amount → DECIMAL(12,2)\\n- gst_amount → DECIMAL(12,2)\\n\\n### reports\\n- file_path → NOT NULL\\n\\n### chat_history\\n- question → NOT NULL\\n- answer → NOT NULL\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 7 — Indexing Strategy\\n\\nInstead of indexing everything, we'll index fields that users search frequently.\\n\\n| Table | Indexed Column | Reason |\\n|--------|----------------|--------|\\n| users | email | Login |\\n| documents | user_id | User documents |\\n| documents | uploaded_at | Recent uploads |\\n| document_analysis | vendor_name | Vendor search |\\n| document_analysis | transaction_date | Date filtering |\\n| document_analysis | category | Category filtering |\\n| reports | user_id | User reports |\\n| chat_history | user_id | Conversation history |\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 8 — Naming Standards\\n\\nWe'll use consistent conventions throughout the project.\\n\\n### Tables\\n\\n```text\\nsnake_case\\nplural nouns\\n```\\n\\nExamples:\\n\\n```text\\nusers\\ndocuments\\nreports\\nchat_history\\ndocument_analysis\\n```\\n\\n### Columns\\n\\n```text\\nsnake_case\\n```\\n\\nExamples:\\n\\n```text\\nvendor_name\\npayment_method\\ntotal_amount\\ncreated_at\\nupdated_at\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 9 — Data Types\\n\\nWe'll standardize data types:\\n\\n| Data | Type |\\n|------|------|\\n| ID | BIGINT UNSIGNED |\\n| Name | VARCHAR(255) |\\n| Email | VARCHAR(255) |\\n| Currency | DECIMAL(12,2) |\\n| Date | DATE |\\n| Timestamp | TIMESTAMP |\\n| Long AI summary | TEXT |\\n| Chat answer | LONGTEXT |\\n\\nThis avoids inconsistencies later.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# STEP 10 — Normalization\\n\\nWe'll explicitly design the database to satisfy:\\n\\n- **1NF**: Atomic values, no repeating groups.\\n- **2NF**: Non-key attributes depend on the whole primary key.\\n- **3NF**: No transitive dependencies.\\n\\nWe'll also include a short explanation of each normal form in the documentation, since this is a common viva question.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 📦 Deliverables for Database Sprint\\n\\nThis sprint will produce:\\n\\n```text\\n05_Database/\\n\\n├── Business_Rules.pdf\\n├── Entity_Description.pdf\\n├── Relationship_Matrix.pdf\\n├── Database_Standards.pdf\\n├── Normalization.pdf\\n├── ER_Diagram.png\\n├── Database_Schema.png\\n├── Data_Dictionary.pdf\\n├── SQL_Schema.sql\\n└── Flask_Model_Mapping.pdf\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 📌 Next Step\\n\\nNow comes one of the most important artifacts in the entire project:\\n\\n### **The ER Diagram**\\n\\nWe're not going to use a generic crow's-foot diagram copied from the internet. We'll create a professional ER diagram that matches the database exactly and later maps directly to our SQLAlchemy models.\\n\\nAfter the ER diagram, we'll immediately generate:\\n1. The SQL schema.\\n2. The Flask model classes.\\n3. The migration plan.\\n\\nFrom that point onward, the backend implementation will be largely a matter of translating the design into code, because the database—the foundation of the application—will already be complete.\",{},{\"_255\":1494,\"_262\":1538,\"_35\":1539,\"_37\":1540,\"_266\":1541,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1542,\"_275\":276},\"9acb234d-e4e0-434f-830f-6ba90ab55278\",[1481],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1547},1785527001.038,1785527016.879163,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1545},{\"_632\":1543,\"_296\":1507,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1508,\"_302\":1508,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1544},[],[1546],\"fine \",{},{\"_255\":1536,\"_262\":1551,\"_35\":1552,\"_37\":1553,\"_266\":1554,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1555,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"30a109d1-6eb2-4efb-8805-162fb5e324e0\",[1494],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1607},1785526952.502772,1785526966.508755,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1605},{\"_279\":1556,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1557,\"_284\":1558,\"_286\":1559,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1560,\"_294\":1561,\"_296\":1562,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1563,\"_302\":1563,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1549,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1604},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1564,\"_581\":1565,\"_583\":1566,\"_585\":1567,\"_587\":1568,\"_589\":1569,\"_591\":1570,\"_593\":1571,\"_1181\":1572,\"_1357\":1573,\"_1359\":1574,\"_1361\":1575,\"_1363\":1576,\"_1365\":1577,\"_1367\":1578,\"_1369\":1579,\"_1371\":1580,\"_1373\":1581,\"_1375\":1582,\"_1377\":1583},[],\"b547bbdd-478c-422f-aa8a-c7cc4bc776b9\",\"21c6aead-ed3e-421e-80da-ce4990a79c8b\",{\"_255\":1603,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1602,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1601,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1600,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1599,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1598,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1597,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1596,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1595,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1594,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1593,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1592,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1591,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1590,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1589,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1588,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1587,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1586,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1585,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},{\"_255\":1584,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"g7z2p5\",\"ig1web\",\"5oh3zw\",\"49276x\",\"oyzz0q\",\"8fp2lm\",\"4tkt0x\",\"ey8rlh\",\"wr9rsa\",\"ez1tqm\",\"mj8tsx\",\"76zhfm\",\"su49xh\",\"dimvjo\",\"o5wazs\",\"awyeky\",\"e36b2g\",\"vm432l\",\"2yltsu\",\"8x84es\",[316],[1606],\"Perfect. I'll keep that as a **project decision**, not something we'll implement immediately.\\n\\n### 📌 Future Decision (Locked)\\nWhen Version 1.0 is complete, we'll design:\\n\\n- Brand identity\\n- Logo\\n- Product name (if we decide to rename FinPilot AI)\\n- Color system\\n- Icons\\n- Typography\\n- Landing page\\n- Marketing website\\n- SaaS dashboard theme\\n- Enterprise UI Kit\\n\\nWe'll treat that as **Product Design Phase**, not College Project Phase.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 🚀 Now let's continue.\\n\\nWe're moving to the most important document in the entire project.\\n\\n# Database Design\\n\\nAlmost every feature depends on it.\\n\\nIf the database is designed well now, coding becomes much easier.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Database Design Roadmap\\n\\n```text\\nStep 1\\nBusiness Objects\\n\\n↓\\n\\nStep 2\\nEntities\\n\\n↓\\n\\nStep 3\\nAttributes\\n\\n↓\\n\\nStep 4\\nRelationships\\n\\n↓\\n\\nStep 5\\nNormalization\\n\\n↓\\n\\nStep 6\\nER Diagram\\n\\n↓\\n\\nStep 7\\nSQL Database\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 1 — Identify Business Objects\\n\\nLet's forget about databases for a moment.\\n\\nInstead, think like a business owner.\\n\\nWhat are the \\\"things\\\" inside our software?\\n\\nI identified these.\\n\\n```text\\nUser\\n\\nDocument\\n\\nInvoice\\n\\nReceipt\\n\\nVendor\\n\\nCategory\\n\\nReport\\n\\nChat\\n\\nAI Insight\\n```\\n\\nNotice something?\\n\\nI intentionally **didn't** put \\\"Database Table.\\\"\\n\\nThese are **Business Objects**.\\n\\nLater they become tables.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 2 — Core Entities\\n\\nFor Version 1.0\\n\\nWe only need these.\\n\\n```text\\nUsers\\n\\nDocuments\\n\\nExtracted_Data\\n\\nReports\\n\\nChat_History\\n```\\n\\nThat's enough to build the MVP.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Future Entities\\n\\nThese will remain in our architecture but **won't be implemented yet**.\\n\\n```text\\nCompanies\\n\\nTeams\\n\\nPermissions\\n\\nNotifications\\n\\nActivity Logs\\n\\nExpense Categories\\n\\nDocument Tags\\n\\nAI Models\\n\\nSubscriptions\\n\\nInvoices\\n\\nPayments\\n\\nIntegrations\\n```\\n\\nWe'll activate them in Version 2.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 3 — Entity Relationships\\n\\nNow let's define relationships.\\n\\n## User\\n\\nOne user\\n\\ncan upload\\n\\nMany documents.\\n\\n```text\\nUser\\n\\n1\\n\\n│\\n\\n│\\n\\n∞\\n\\nDocuments\\n```\\n\\nRelationship\\n\\n```text\\nOne-to-Many\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Documents\\n\\nEach document\\n\\nafter AI processing\\n\\ncreates\\n\\none structured record.\\n\\n```text\\nDocument\\n\\n1\\n\\n│\\n\\n│\\n\\n1\\n\\nExtracted Data\\n```\\n\\nRelationship\\n\\n```text\\nOne-to-One\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### User\\n\\nOne user\\n\\ncan ask\\n\\nmany AI questions.\\n\\n```text\\nUser\\n\\n1\\n\\n│\\n\\n│\\n\\n∞\\n\\nChat History\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### User\\n\\nOne user\\n\\ncan generate\\n\\nmany reports.\\n\\n```text\\nUser\\n\\n1\\n\\n│\\n\\n│\\n\\n∞\\n\\nReports\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Complete Relationship\\n\\n```text\\nUser\\n│\\n├──────────────┐\\n│              │\\n│              │\\n▼              ▼\\n\\nDocuments     Chat History\\n│\\n│\\n▼\\n\\nExtracted Data\\n│\\n▼\\n\\nReports\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 4 — Database Naming Convention\\n\\nWe'll follow professional naming standards.\\n\\nTables\\n\\n```text\\nusers\\n\\ndocuments\\n\\nextracted_data\\n\\nreports\\n\\nchat_history\\n```\\n\\nAll lowercase.\\n\\nSnake_case.\\n\\nPlural table names.\\n\\nThis matches common SQL style guides.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 5 — Primary Keys\\n\\nEvery table gets\\n\\n```sql\\nid\\n```\\n\\nAuto Increment\\n\\nBIGINT\\n\\nReason\\n\\nFuture scalability.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 6 — Foreign Keys\\n\\nDocuments\\n\\ncontains\\n\\n```text\\nuser_id\\n```\\n\\nExtracted Data\\n\\ncontains\\n\\n```text\\ndocument_id\\n```\\n\\nReports\\n\\ncontains\\n\\n```text\\nuser_id\\n```\\n\\nChat\\n\\ncontains\\n\\n```text\\nuser_id\\n```\\n\\nVery simple.\\n\\nVery scalable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Step 7 — Standard Columns\\n\\nEvery table gets\\n\\n```text\\ncreated_at\\n\\nupdated_at\\n```\\n\\nThis is something many student projects forget.\\n\\nLater\\n\\nAudit logs\\n\\nbecome much easier.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Database Standards\\n\\nWe will enforce:\\n\\n- Primary Keys\\n- Foreign Keys\\n- Indexes\\n- Unique Constraints\\n- NOT NULL constraints\\n- Default Values\\n- Cascade Delete (only where appropriate)\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Normalization\\n\\nWe'll design up to **Third Normal Form (3NF)**.\\n\\nWhy?\\n\\n- No duplicate data.\\n- Better consistency.\\n- Easier maintenance.\\n- Industry standard.\\n\\nThis is an excellent point to discuss in your viva.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# 📋 Database Design Deliverables\\n\\nAfter this section, you'll receive:\\n\\n```text\\n05_Database/\\n\\nBusiness_Objects.pdf\\n\\nEntity_List.pdf\\n\\nRelationship_Document.pdf\\n\\nNormalization.pdf\\n\\nDatabase_Standards.pdf\\n\\nER_Diagram.png\\n\\nDatabase_Schema.pdf\\n\\nSQL_Script.sql\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# ⚠️ One Design Decision I'd Like to Make\\n\\nBefore we draw the ER Diagram, I'd like to make one architectural improvement that will help both the college project and the future SaaS.\\n\\nInstead of calling the AI output table **`extracted_data`**, I'd like to name it:\\n\\n```text\\ndocument_analysis\\n```\\n\\nWhy?\\n\\nBecause today it stores:\\n\\n- Vendor\\n- Amount\\n- GST\\n- Date\\n\\nBut tomorrow it can also store:\\n\\n- AI Summary\\n- Risk Score\\n- Duplicate Detection\\n- Category Confidence\\n- Business Insights\\n- Fraud Flags\\n\\nThe name **`document_analysis`** is broader and future-proof, while still making sense for Version 1.0.\\n\\nI recommend we adopt this naming now so we never have to rename the table later. It keeps the architecture cleaner and more extensible without making the MVP any more complex.\",{},{\"_255\":1549,\"_262\":1611,\"_35\":1612,\"_37\":1613,\"_266\":1614,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1615,\"_275\":276},\"70ce1605-527d-49ac-8d57-b5a7168b0204\",[1536],{\"_322\":376,\"_273\":1620},1785526952.086,1785526966.784469,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1618},{\"_632\":1616,\"_296\":1562,\"_373\":-5,\"_300\":1563,\"_302\":1563,\"_288\":289,\"_306\":10,\"_304\":14},{\"_634\":1617},[],[1619],\"yeah but we will decide that after wards keep that in mind also so lets continue\",{},{\"_255\":1609,\"_262\":1624,\"_35\":1625,\"_37\":1626,\"_266\":1627,\"_268\":269,\"_270\":26,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1628,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":278},\"0db3ee01-80cc-4636-aabc-4f6e7777088d\",[1549],{\"_322\":323,\"_273\":1642},1785525964.870663,1785525975.045916,{\"_317\":318,\"_319\":1640},{\"_279\":1629,\"_281\":26,\"_282\":1630,\"_284\":1631,\"_286\":1632,\"_288\":289,\"_290\":291,\"_292\":1633,\"_294\":1634,\"_296\":1635,\"_298\":299,\"_300\":1636,\"_302\":1636,\"_303\":289,\"_47\":48,\"_304\":26,\"_305\":1622,\"_306\":10},{\"_31\":313,\"_314\":1639},[],[],[],{\"_307\":1637},[],\"06cdc143-6f0d-43da-a503-09a60c9c13a3\",\"6d4f3db9-75f4-42ae-90ca-b05807c3b924\",{\"_255\":1638,\"_310\":14,\"_311\":14,\"_312\":-5},\"n5tdb0\",[316],[1641],\"Excellent! We've officially started producing the project deliverables.\\n\\nI've created the **first Design Pack (v1)** containing the initial architecture documents.\\n\\n### 📦 Download\\n[**📁 FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v1.zip**](sandbox:/mnt/data/FinPilot_AI_Design_Pack_v1.zip)\\n\\n### Current Contents\\n\\n```\\n01_System_Architecture/\\n├── Overall_System_Architecture.png\\n├── Overall_System_Architecture.pdf\\n├── Three_Tier_Architecture.png\\n├── Three_Tier_Architecture.pdf\\n├── Module_Architecture.png\\n├── Module_Architecture.pdf\\n├── AI_Architecture.png\\n└── AI_Architecture.pdf\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## This is only Version 1\\n\\nThese diagrams establish the basic architecture, but they're not yet at the level I ultimately want for your project.\\n\\n### My goal is to create diagrams comparable to those found in:\\n\\n- Microsoft architecture documentation\\n- AWS solution architecture guides\\n- Enterprise software design documents\\n- Professional IEEE software engineering reports\\n\\nThat means:\\n\\n- High-quality icons\\n- Professional color coding\\n- Clean alignment and spacing\\n- Proper UML notation\\n- Consistent branding across every diagram\\n- Report-ready resolution (300 DPI or better)\\n- SVG, PNG, and PDF outputs\\n\\n---\\n\\n## What happens next\\n\\nThe next package will be much larger and more detailed.\\n\\n### UML Package\\n- Use Case Diagram\\n- Use Case Specification\\n- Activity Diagram\\n- Sequence Diagram\\n- Class Diagram\\n- Component Diagram\\n- Deployment Diagram\\n- State Diagram\\n\\n### Database Package\\n- ER Diagram\\n- Normalized Schema\\n- Data Dictionary\\n- SQL Schema\\n\\n### DFD Package\\n- Context Diagram\\n- Level 0\\n- Level 1\\n- Level 2\\n\\n### UI/UX Package\\n- Login\\n- Register\\n- Dashboard\\n- Upload\\n- Documents\\n- AI Chat\\n- Reports\\n- Settings\\n- Profile\\n\\n---\\n\\n## One improvement I'd like to make\\n\\nRather than using generic diagram styles, I want to create a **custom visual identity** for the entire project.\\n\\nFor example:\\n\\n- A **FinPilot AI logo**.\\n- A professional **blue-and-white design language**.\\n- Consistent icons for User, AI, Database, OCR, Reports, and Documents.\\n- Every PDF, diagram, and document carrying the same branding.\\n\\nThe result will look less like a typical college submission and more like documentation from a real software product. That consistency will also make your final report and presentation much more impressive.\\n\\nFrom this point onward, every diagram and document we produce will follow that same design system and will be included in the milestone ZIP packages automatically.\",{},{\"_255\":1622,\"_262\":1646,\"_35\":1647,\"_37\":1648,\"_266\":1649,\"_268\":269,\"_271\":272,\"_273\":1650,\"_275\":276,\"_277\":405},\"d7c68519-ebc2-413c-9a1c-9a75abf77fd0\",[1609],{\"_322\":455,\"_440\":456,\"_273\":1671},1785525963.1755133,1785525964.5704913,{\"_317\":454,\"_318\":1665},{\"_281\":26,\"_406\":1651,\"_296\"